{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1481645-pugmire-fish-species","id":1481645,"title":"Pugmire fish species?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-21T23:46:01-07:00","id":1481645,"title":"Pugmire fish species?","content":"I like how the pugmire games focus on family pets, and having the family pet go on adventures. My niece's turtle, no problem. Even ferrets and hamsters are thematically easy enough. But what about fish? They are briefly mentioned, and are supposed to rule the seas - but do they have hands? How do they interact with the other species?<br /> Not dogfish, catfish, or ratskates, but Fishfish - what is Eddy Webb planning to do with the gilled swimming creature sitting on my shelf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T07:46:55-07:00","id":1481662,"title":"","content":"At least on official rules for Fishes, we do not have any in books. No rumors of them were shown to this date. However, Onyx Path started to make big gamelines announcement on their<b> <a href=\"https://startplaying.games/event/onyx-path\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Con</a></b>, that in this year, is as 10th till 12th June on <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">OPP Twitch</a> channel. Probably new book for <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> will be announced then - that's how was announced <b>Squeaks in the Deep</b> in 2021. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2022, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T07:54:45-07:00","id":1481663,"title":"","content":"For Fishes fan rules, you are in luck - new Species rules are generally straight forward. Only need how to 'divide' Specie on 'Subspecies' ( factions ) and give them Ability modifier and one Inner Knack. Look on Breeds in Pugmire, Houses in Mau - and you can look on our totally fan created <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1475986-rop-fan-playable-badgers-and-other-species\">Tribes for Badgers, ferrets, wolverines, etc.</a> ( Also given extra Hamsters Species for Squeaks Rodents Upbringings. ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If has some semi-logical Subspecies divide for Fishes, you can make them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T08:03:31-07:00","id":1481664,"title":"","content":"For inspiration, I can advise <b>ThunderCats 2011</b> series - great for <b>Mau</b>, cause about literal animal kingdoms created after Man - there are humanoid 'sand Fishes' in episode or two, interesting ones. Here is trailer for the series<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yevav-RcUfQ\" data-code=\"Yevav-RcUfQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Yevav-RcUfQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Here is graphics for Fishman from series<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSiU8IopQTMX0qwBDrxZ9RszxRhZaHjdUY2iQ4332hddvxaE3k0JvEbz01fnJIQbW7zLSM&amp;usqp=CAU\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2022, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T00:33:31-07:00","id":1481733,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the thundercats interpretation. I think if Eddy was going to go that route, fish would have shown up in Pirates of Pugmire, at least as enemies or rivals. And there's nothing! I hope you're right and they announce something at Onyx Path Con.<br /> <br /> Maybe Eddie hasn't decided how they fit into the world yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T07:11:09-07:00","id":1481918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1481645-pugmire-fish-species#post1481645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not dogfish, catfish, or ratskates, but Fishfish - what is Eddy Webb planning to do with the gilled swimming creature sitting on my shelf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now, I don't have any plans. I thought I was going to, but I keep running into what I call &quot;the Aquaman problem&quot;: i.e., either you have to set an entire chronicle underwater (thus basically making it a different game), or you have to give them so much to do on land that the fact that they're fish is largely moot and they're just another land-dwelling species. It's something I mull over now and then, but I don't have any current plans to announce anything at Onyx Path Con regarding our finny friends. Sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T16:16:09-07:00","id":1481956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1481645-pugmire-fish-species?p=1481918#post1481918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right now, I don't have any plans. I thought I was going to, but I keep running into what I call &quot;the Aquaman problem&quot;: i.e., either you have to set an entire chronicle underwater (thus basically making it a different game), or you have to give them so much to do on land that the fact that they're fish is largely moot and they're just another land-dwelling species. It's something I mull over now and then, but I don't have any current plans to announce anything at Onyx Path Con regarding our finny friends. Sorry!</div> </div> </div> </div>purely anecdotal but my group have chatted a lot about wanting more material on aquatic fantasy settings with their own compelling hooks. So while the Aquaman problem arises with him in the Justice League, he still can shine in his own title with the occasional crossover. Just my 2 cents for whatever that\u2019s worth with current inflation<br /> <br /> Edit: I just realized referencing story \u201chooks\u201d is probably insensitive when discussing the fishfolk. My apologies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-26-2022, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T05:50:57-07:00","id":1482593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1481645-pugmire-fish-species?p=1481956#post1481956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> purely anecdotal but my group have chatted a lot about wanting more material on aquatic fantasy settings with their own compelling hooks. So while the Aquaman problem arises with him in the Justice League, he still can shine in his own title with the occasional crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why I call it the Aquaman problem. I love Aquaman in his own book (I have a decent run of his New 52 comic), but more often he gets pulled into Justice League rather than characters from Justice League getting pulled into his book.<br /> <br /> Thus, any fish book would have to be an entire chronicle book (effectively its own game) with minimal connections to Pugmire or Monarchies of Mau. And, honestly, people are more into dogs and cats than fish. It's something I'm still poking at off and on, but right now a purely aquatic setting is more in the realm of a really cool Canis Minor project than something I'm likely to tackle in the near future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T07:36:11-07:00","id":1482604,"title":"","content":"So... kind of a tangential question:<br /> <br /> I've had some vague thoughts about how to world build in fish in a way that can integrate with dogs and cats, but the Aquaman problem persists once the focus zooms down to playable characters. Basically, I can come up what fish NPCs would be doing around the other uplifted animals, but I can't see that translating into Callings that provide a meaningfully unique play experience mixed with the rest of the available ones out there.<br /> <br /> This also feels a bit backwards from how I'd normally think up this sort of thing, but...<br /> <br /> What kind of magic do fish have? A lot of the RoP casters help emphasize a lot about the different playable groups. Dogs have the old school Aristans = arcane Shepherds = divine division that helps stress the strong cultural unifying force of the kingdom. Cats use a lot of &quot;hybrid&quot; casters that are more individualistic that plays into how cats are social but on their terms. Lizard alchemy might is a bit less defined in this sense but certainly fits the idea of cold blood creatures that are more methodical and prepared. Rodents are obviously super defined by being the psionics of the setting and how that plays back into their past with humans.<br /> <br /> So... I feel like if I had some idea of what fish magic was, I'd have a better idea of what themes are at play besides &quot;do underwater stuff,&quot; that could refine my bigger world building stuff into the start of something playable in RoP as it exists. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T09:14:02-07:00","id":1482609,"title":"","content":"Maybe 'nature magic' for fishes - like druids? It would work a bit with <b>Pirates of Pugmire</b> assumptions already, as <b><i>Mystic</i></b> from <b>PoP</b> is already 'sea druid' Calling for cats... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:23:56-07:00","id":1482659,"title":"","content":"I had thought about that, but I ran into two issues. First, it pushes them farther away from integration into dog or cat society by making their magic defined by being something that pushes them away from social centers. So basically fish druids just further the Aquaman problem. Second I suspect it would also end up overlapping too much with Badgers as I can't help but assume them getting a significant expansion would mean getting a Calling that leans into this because Badgers are already defined in the setting by their anti-urban life style.<br /> <br /> My pondering lead me closer to something like the Loremaster prestige class from D&amp;D 3e or Oracles from Pathfinder, but that's very early mental rumination.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}